{
 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed 2 of the 5 cases it was looking for, on two different scenes. On 096988dd the policy failed every run with the car 0.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed and the ego at 1.2x (S13). On 19f339ba it failed every run with the car as recorded and the ego at 1.2x (S40). For both, the 90% range sits above 0.5, but each rests on only a few repeats, so the true rate could be anywhere from moderate to certain. Neither failure comes from the retimed car cutting in or slowing ahead. In every failed run the policy drifted left out of its lane, against its route command or with a clear road ahead (on 19f339ba after braking hard for no reason), and hit a car in the next lane. That car was not the one being retimed. The video review blamed the policy in every failure, and none looks like a simulator artifact. No other combination failed on the other six scenes the study tried, and one scene in the plan (1c45ce3a) was never run, so the other three cases were not found within the budget.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, with the car 0.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed and the ego at 1.2x, the policy failed every run. The 90% range lies above 0.5, so this case is confirmed.",
    "settings": [
     "S13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba, with the car at its recorded timing and speed and the ego at 1.2x, the policy failed every run. The 90% range lies above 0.5, so this case is confirmed. Raising only the ego's speed was enough here.",
    "settings": [
     "S40"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Both confirmed failures are the policy's own lateral errors rather than reactions to the retimed car. On 096988dd its plan bent left against a RIGHT or STRAIGHT route command, and it hit vehicle 41 in the left lane. On 19f339ba it braked hard with the lead car far ahead and pulling away, drifted left and clipped actor 1 in the left lane. Rear contacts in the 19f339ba runs came after the at-fault front hit.",
    "settings": [
     "S13",
     "S40"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The failures seem to need the 1.2x ego speed. Single runs at neighbouring settings did not fail: the same car timing at ego 1.0x on 096988dd, the unshifted car at ego 1.2x on 096988dd, and ego 1.4x or a car shifted 1 s earlier on 19f339ba. These are single runs, so they are hints, not rates.",
    "settings": [
     "S12",
     "S14",
     "S39",
     "S41"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Settings that were repeated and never failed are unlikely to fail at more than half their runs. These are 023b7fcc with the car 0.5 s later at recorded speed, 12855a41 with the cut-in car 2 s earlier at 2x and the ego at 1.2x, and 023b7fcc with the car 1 s earlier at 1.5x.",
    "settings": [
